    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return `selfLink = \"/api/owners/\" + <owner id>` on the owner response. Rather than duplicate the string in the two responder functions (which already only patch `bulkSignupWarning`), I treated `selfLink` as a **derived DTO field**, matching how every other computed owner field (`salutation`, `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, \u2026) is handled. That puts the logic in one place and covers both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and `POST /api/owners` automatically.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` response schema (right after `id`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setSelfLink`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` plus a small `selfLink(Owner)` default method returning `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`, or `null` before an id is assigned (guarding against the nullable `Integer` id).\n\nNo responder or YAML pipeline changes were needed \u2014 the mapper feeds every owner response.",
